  "details": "It would be nice to have a launch option to have the displayName also include the playerId.\n\nSomething like: `--show-player-ids`\n\nFor example when running Udon code for `Networking.LocalPlayer.displayName` it would return \"BobyStar 1\". You can also see this applied to the nameplate above their head.\n\nThis would bring problems to those who want to test via displayName, which is why I propose a launch option to enable this behavior. If necessary this can be exclusive to Build & Test (non-EAC verified clients).\n\nThis is useful for creators who want to tell between their Build & Test clients without having to temporarily add code to include the player id with the display name. Making the process of checking which client is which quick by glancing at their nameplate.\n\nYou can tell which player is which via Debug Menu 8 but you cannot see the local player's id, meaning you'd have to cross check with another client.",
